vacancies.appmethod:
Applicants must apply online through the G.F. 340 Online Application System of the Civil Service Bureau (https://www.csb.gov.hk) not later than 13 November 2026.

Applicants are required to submit copies of (1) official transcripts and certificates of academic/professional qualifications, including results achieved in Chinese and English languages; (2) proof of working experience (including current and past employment showing the positions, commencement dates, and end dates or current employment status); and (3) result notification letter or electronic result certificates of Basic Law and National Security Law Test (if any) by e-mail to "appt@archsd.gov.hk" on or before 20 November 2026.  Please quote "Application for the post of Survey Officer (Quantity)" and your on-line application number on the subject of e-mail and each page of the copies of the supporting documents.

Your application will NOT be considered if:
(a) the application is late or incomplete;
(b) the Application Form is submitted in person, by post, by fax or email;
(c) the application fails to provide the information required in the prescribed Application Form for consideration of your application;
(d) the application is submitted without copy of supporting documents as required; and
(e) it is not clear from your statements that you have met the entry requirements for this position.

Applicants are encouraged to provide their email address(es) on the application forms.  Candidates who are selected for interview will normally receive an invitation (by email or by post) in about six to eight weeks from the closing date for application.  Those who are not invited for interview may assume that their applications are unsuccessful.

